2 Analyzing Risk
-------------------------


Learning Outcomes
Having completed this module you will be able to:
Discuss analyzing organizational risk and the business impact of risk.
List the phases of risk management.
Define BIA (Business Impact Analysis).
Describe the impact scenarios.
Explain the meaning of the term Maximum Tolerable Downtime (MTD).
Underline the guidelines used when performing business impact analysis.

Lesson Summary
Analyzing risk plays a big role in making sure you have a secure environment in your organization.
By assessing and identifying particular risk and damage it can cause, you can mitigate these threats and establish the right corrective measurements to avoid possible damage to people and systems.
Business Impact Analysis (BIA) is a systematic activity that identifies organizational risks and determines their impact on ongoing business-critical operations and processes.
Impact scenarios describe how life, property, safety, finances and reputation can be affected.
Maximum Tolerable Downtime (MTD) is the longest time period that a business outage can occur without causing irrecoverable business failure.
Privacy assessments consist of Privacy impact assessment (PIA), Privacy threshold assessment (PTA) and Personally identifiable information (PII).
When performing business impact analysis one should identify mission-essential functions and critical system, as well as identify impact scenarios and calculate MTD, RTO, MTTF, MTTR and MTBF.

